{% macro ship_shape(stack) %}
## What this cycle ships

{% if stack %}
The cycle ships one commit per PR of the design's **Stack** section, in
stack order, each on its own branch. The designer decides the split, and nothing ships
outside it: no PR the section does not name, no second commit inside a PR,
no other order. A request or design that dictates a different commit shape
specifies something this workflow will not produce.
{% else %}
The cycle lands as **one commit per repository in scope**, on that
repository's launch branch, in the **Scope** section's ship order: within a
repository every round is squashed, and the ship gate squashes all rounds
into one. No intermediate commit, branch or ordering survives inside a
repository. A request or design that specifies several commits in one
repository, separate PRs, or an order other than the pin order specifies
something this workflow cannot produce. Another workflow ships work as
several reviewable commits; this is not it.
{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
